TEXT -1232 -648 Left 2 !.tran 5 startup
TEXT -376 -208 Left 2 ;the opamp Vcc should be\nthe same as the input voltage
TEXT 24 728 Left 2 ;Use opamps specialized in comparation\nThe switching time should be fast so\nfast microchanges in current can be\nregistered
TEXT -808 -696 Left 2 ;This mosfet should have lower Rdson\nthant the R1 resistor, so it not jeopardize\nthe high current sense
TEXT 224 -392 Left 2 ;This High current sense should\nconsidewr the RdsON from the\nmosfet
TEXT -888 976 Left 2 ;The MID lead to the opamp should be folowed by\nan buffer, so the following voltage divider cannot\nsource current from the sense path
TEXT -1424 720 Left 2 ;The INA- and MID values can be very small\nwhen current is at uA. In that sense, the\ndiferential amplifier must also amplify\nthe difference by 1000
TEXT 456 -16 Left 2 ;Current source in parallel with Zener diode.\nThis prevents the high voltage spikes that\nthe current source induces.\n \nOne source for full scale variations and\none from low current variations
TEXT -784 240 Left 2 ;Heads up at the opamp selection:\n \n- Buffers OpAmps should have low bias and leakage\n  current so it doesn't affect the readings\n \n- Diferentiator OpAmp should have low input offset\n  voltage and High bandwidth so the 1000 amplification\n  doesn't harm the system bandwidth.\n  Consider using cascated 31.1 gain OpAmps
